    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the context before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Unused imports cluttering the file\n- The expected value `2 + 3 * 256 + 4 * 256 * 256` is raw arithmetic with no explanation of the little-endian encoding\n- The 4th byte `5` in the stream is silently ignored (only 3 bytes are read)\n- No clear explanation of what the test verifies\n\nLet me write the improved test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports, extracts the expected value into a named variable, and adds inline comments that explain the little-endian byte layout step-by-step — making it immediately clear why each byte contributes its specific amount to the result."
